- C5: FACT — No source-local tautology in a reported effect, because no effect is reported (`result.harmful_side_read: false`, no TPR/FPR/CI anywhere); INFERENCE risk (not a violation): task-truth identity is defined via the same canonicalizer the remedy targets (contract §5, `d3.unique_canonical` / `mp.map_headers`), so a future POSITIVE would be partly definitional — see Finding 4.
- C6: FACT — No label/stage/outcome leakage observed: `harmful_semantic_read_utc: null`, `harmful_side_read: false`, admission uses no score/label/harmful read (contract §6), injection map used only as a frozen exclusion (`excluded_injected_uid: 95`), candidate order is a frozen rule-order enumeration; INFERENCE residual: the inherited fold map enumerates clean ∪ harmful UIDs, so split assignment depends on the *presence* of harmful UIDs (not their outcomes).
